to-be-incorporated-into-paper-71 : List Word
to-be-incorporated-into-paper-71 = unlines (cons "**Dimensions.** How the dimensions of the object language are held in lib/nbe.cub is answered by the standard semantics; it was never a question for Avik." (cons "- In CCHM a term in Γ; Ψ; φ means a family natural in the stage: an element of A at every Ψ′ with a" (cons "  substitution Ψ′ → Ψ satisfying φ, commuting with every further substitution." (cons "- A dimension's value at a stage is an element of the free De Morgan algebra on that stage's names," (cons "  and the substitutions are maps of that algebra. This is the cubical-set model." (cons "- So the number of dimensions varies only in the quantification over stages. A semantic action of" (cons "  interval expressions, defined on syntax, must be shown once to respect the algebra's equations." (cons "  That is the well-definedness of the cube category's action, not a cost of the encoding." (cons "- `lib/nbe.cub` is that model inside the host:" (cons "  - stages are host cubes (`Cube n`);" (cons "  - interval expressions are data (`IEx`, `DNF`);" (cons "  - substitutions are `Sub` and `cmap-d`." (cons "- Its steps map onto the obligations:" (cons "  - F2a–F2c are the well-definedness (every De Morgan law, with no 2-cell);" (cons "  - F2d is the normalizer's soundness;" (cons "  - F2d′ is the normalizer's canonicity;" (cons "  - F2e is naturality in substitutions." (cons "- Holding an object dimension as a host interval variable is not available, because the host's" (cons "  interval is not a type (`I × Nat` is refused), and it would only move these obligations anyway." (cons "- So lib/nbe.cub is kept and continues at F2d, the normalizer's soundness." nil))))))))))))))))))))
